{#
  Sub-navigation of one article's management pages — Édition, Aperçu,
  Réponses, and (once the form delivers a ticket) Scanner un billet, with
  Finance pushed to the far end.

  It used to draw its own `nav nav-pills` row, one of the last two places
  in the application still doing so. The site's component is
  partials/page_picker.html.twig, whose docblock carries the history: six
  places copied the same boilerplate, a seventh drew primary pills, two
  modules used nav-pills. Chips remain wrong for a sub-navigation — a
  chip reads as a filter you toggle — so the shape is the nav rail,
  Bootstrap `nav nav-underline` (design.md §7.6).

  `current_path` is SYNTHETIC here, computed from `active` rather than
  read off the request: Édition and Aperçu are the same route, told apart
  only by `?tab=preview`, and the picker matches on the whole `url`
  string. Same trick as groups/list.html.twig.

  Nothing at all is rendered before the article's first save: there is no
  second view to navigate to yet, and a one-tab rail linking to
  "/news//gerer" would 404.

  Parameters:
  - `article_id`         — null until the article is first saved.
  - `active`             — 'edit' | 'preview' | 'responses' | 'scan'.
  - `can_view_responses` — presentation only; the route keeps its own
                           floor (SECURITY.md §3).
  - `form_id`            — optional, required by the scan tab.
  - `issues_ticket`      — optional: the form delivers a ticket, so the
                           scan page exists for it.
  - `finance_link`       — optional: the « Paiements attendus » URL, set
                           by the controller only when the finance module
                           is on AND the viewer may open that page
                           (role_min: intendant). A tab pointing at a 403
                           is worse than no tab.
#}
{% if article_id %}
    {% set _base = '/news/' ~ article_id ~ '/gerer' %}
    {% set _responses = '/news/' ~ article_id ~ '/form/responses' %}
    {% set _scan = '/news/scan/' ~ (form_id|default(0)) %}
    {% set _pages = [
        { url: _base, label: 'Édition' },
        { url: _base ~ '?tab=preview', label: 'Aperçu' },
    ] %}
    {% if can_view_responses %}
        {% set _pages = _pages|merge([{ url: _responses, label: 'Réponses' }]) %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if issues_ticket|default(false) and form_id|default(0) %}
        {% set _pages = _pages|merge([{ url: _scan, label: 'Scanner un billet', icon: 'bi-qr-code-scan' }]) %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if finance_link|default(null) %}
        {% set _pages = _pages|merge([{ url: finance_link, label: 'Finance', icon: 'bi-cash-coin', align_end: true }]) %}
    {% endif %}
    {% include 'partials/page_picker.html.twig' with {
        picker_id: 'news-form-tabs',
        pages: _pages,
        current_path: active == 'preview' ? _base ~ '?tab=preview'
            : (active == 'responses' ? _responses
            : (active == 'scan' ? _scan : _base)),
        aria_label: "Pages de l'article",
    } only %}
{% endif %}
